WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.840
In October 2022, inflation
hit 11.1 per cent in the UK,

2
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.930
and 10.6 per cent in the euro area.

3
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:11.710
Central banks reached for one main tool.

4
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:15.240
They raised interest
rates, again and again.

5
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:18.880
In the UK, Bank Rate
climbed from 0.1 per cent

6
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.330
to 5.25 per cent.

7
00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:23.280
But how can one interest rate,

8
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.870
set by a handful of people round a table,

9
00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.170
slow down inflation
across a whole country?

10
00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.610
In this mission, you'll
follow the chain from one

11
00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.340
rate decision to the prices in the shops.

12
00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:37.030
Then you'll take control in a graph lab:

13
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:41.060
set the rate, and watch output
and the price level respond.

14
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:44.450
Your mission: explain how a
single rate decision reaches

15
00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:46.520
prices right across the economy.
